<!--
  COMMISSION_LEDGER_CLEANUP_1 (poison_forest sheet slug
  `toxic-prized-meat-def-property-on-the-4-flagged-keepers-neeb`).
  poison_forest.md §7 "Uniquely available": "Toxic exotic meat. Every animal
  here is poisonous and a delicacy: these are the prestige ingredients for
  the Star Wars cuisine chain, the things a cook brags about surviving.
  Danger and value in the same carcass." rosters/poison_forest.json's own
  fauna list flags exactly four keepers `toxic-prized-meat carrier`: Neebray
  (small-flier, donor `mlie.starwarsanimalcollection`), RSW_Screecher
  (medium-pred, ours — ROSTER_DEAD_BMT_NAMES_SWEEP_1 renamed this row from
  the slug's own stale `BMT_Screecher`), Visceral (medium-pred, donor
  `mlie.horrors`), AA_Helixien (giant, donor `sarg.alphaanimals`).

  mechanic_load reads "meat hediff def, no C#" — matched exactly: the toxic
  half reuses `VanillaAnimalsExpandedWaste.IngestionOutcomeDoer_Toxic`, a
  donor C# class already absorbed wholesale into this mod's own Assemblies/
  (Absorbed_VAEWasteMegatardi_Defs.xml's own header explains the carry-
  forward), already live in this exact mod for VAEWaste_ToxicMeat — zero new
  C#. The prized half is `preferability RawTasty` (rather than the vanilla
  meat generator's default RawBad) plus a positive taste thought
  (RUT_PoisonForestMeatThoughts.xml) and an above-market MarketValue,
  instead of the VAEWaste precedent's negative "disgusting" thought — this
  biome's meat is a bragging-rights delicacy, not a last resort.

  Engine mechanism verified before authoring: `ThingDefGenerator_Meat`
  (RimWorld/ThingDefGenerator_Meat.cs) only auto-generates a race's meat def
  when `race.specificMeatDef == null` — so a hand-authored meat ThingDef plus
  `<race><specificMeatDef>` on the race (see
  Patches/PoisonForest_ToxicPrizedMeat.xml, same folder) is the only route;
  patching a "Meat_Neebray"-style node directly would silently do nothing,
  because no such XML node exists to patch (RimWorld generates it at
  load time, after patches resolve). Shape follows this mod family's own
  precedent for a hand-authored specificMeatDef target,
  RM_StockedPoolMeats.xml (ParentName="OrganicProductBase", explicit
  ingestible/comps/thingCategories rather than a nonexistent "MeatBase"
  parent) and VAEWaste_ToxicMeat's outcomeDoer wiring above it.

  Placeholder art: vanilla meat stack textures (Meat_Small/Meat_Big by body
  size, same convention ThingDefGenerator_Meat itself and RM_StockedPoolMeats
  both use), retinted per species — no new PNGs, no artpipe job needed.
-->
<Defs>

  <ThingDef ParentName="OrganicProductBase">
    <defName>RUT_NeebrayMeat</defName>
    <label>neebray meat</label>
    <description>Thin, silica-veined meat off a neebray, carrying the same metal-rich tailings the whole biome sweats out. Nobody eats it plain — a cook works it the way you'd work a fish that could kill you, and the reputation for surviving the dish travels further than the dish itself does.</description>
    <graphicData>
      <texPath>Things/Item/Resource/MeatFoodRaw/Meat_Small</texPath>
      <graphicClass>Graphic_StackCount</graphicClass>
      <color>(70, 60, 75)</color>
    </graphicData>
    <thingCategories>
      <li>MeatRaw</li>
    </thingCategories>
    <statBases>
      <MaxHitPoints>60</MaxHitPoints>
      <MarketValue>9</MarketValue>
      <Mass>0.02</Mass>
      <Flammability>0.5</Flammability>
      <DeteriorationRate>6</DeteriorationRate>
      <Nutrition>0.05</Nutrition>
      <FoodPoisonChanceFixedHuman>0.02</FoodPoisonChanceFixedHuman>
    </statBases>
    <socialPropernessMatters>true</socialPropernessMatters>
    <ingestible>
      <foodType>Meat</foodType>
      <preferability>RawTasty</preferability>
      <ingestEffect>EatMeat</ingestEffect>
      <ingestSound>RawMeat_Eat</ingestSound>
      <specialThoughtDirect>RUT_AtePoisonForestMeatDirect</specialThoughtDirect>
      <specialThoughtAsIngredient>RUT_AtePoisonForestMeatAsIngredient</specialThoughtAsIngredient>
      <outcomeDoers>
        <li Class="VanillaAnimalsExpandedWaste.IngestionOutcomeDoer_Toxic">
          <severity>0.05</severity>
        </li>
      </outcomeDoers>
    </ingestible>
    <comps>
      <li Class="CompProperties_Rottable">
        <daysToRotStart>2</daysToRotStart>
        <rotDestroys>true</rotDestroys>
      </li>
    </comps>
    <tickerType>Rare</tickerType>
  </ThingDef>

